  "command": "python run_chunk_sweep.py --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-2b --out .; python run_chunk_sweep.py --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-9b --out 9b; python run_chunk_sweep.py --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-4b --out 4b (three fresh processes per chunk, each `python -m kindi bench --split-at 4096,8192 --split-generated 128 --sample-vram --json`, KINDI_CTX=8320, KINDI_CHUNK=<chunk>); KINDI_CHUNK=1024 python -m kindi --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-4b verify; KINDI_CHUNK=1024 python -m kindi --pack ~/.kindi/packs/bonsai-9b verify",
  "notes": "The 2B's fastest cell at both prompt lengths remains 256, already the default. The 4B fits the same 8,320 context and its fastest cell is 1024: 3.1-3.5% ahead of 512 and 7.0-8.2% ahead of 256, at +138/+204 MiB sampled peak. The 9B's fastest cell is 1024, 1.0-1.4% ahead of 512 and 9.5-11.2% ahead of 256. No global default change: 256 remains the 2B optimum and a global 1024 would make the 2B 1.6-1.7% slower at +159 MiB peak; 1024 is a 4B/9B per-model/autotune candidate, and 27B remains unmeasured. The page carries p95, the per-pass rows and the sampled peaks; the roadmap quotes the 2B/4B/9B p50 cells, the 4B peak pair and the three verify results.",
